From: Allen Blaylock <alblay.lhs@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 18:40:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] core: detect 32 bit ARM via the canonical __ARM_ARCH macro

qglobal.h only recognizes the exact macros __ARM_ARCH_7__, __ARM_ARCH_6__
and __ARM_ARCH_5__, but GCC defines a profile-specific spelling instead:
building for cortex-a15 defines __ARM_ARCH_7A__ (verified against the
Yocto cortexa15t2hf toolchain; armv7ve builds define __ARM_ARCH_7VE__),
none of which match, so any 32-bit ARM profile beyond base v7 dies with
"#error Unsupported system architecture, CopperSpice requires V5 or
newer". Check __ARM_ARCH first - the canonical numeric architecture
macro defined by GCC 4.8+ and Clang for every ARM target - and keep the
old exact-match tests as a fallback for ancient compilers. The stray
Q_PROCESSOR_ARM_V8 in the v6 branch (upstream typo for V6) is left
untouched; none of the Q_PROCESSOR_ARM_V* macros have any users.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/core/global/qglobal.h | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/core/global/qglobal.h b/src/core/global/qglobal.h
--- a/src/core/global/qglobal.h
+++ b/src/core/global/qglobal.h
@@ -101,15 +101,15 @@
 
 #   define Q_PROCESSOR_ARM_32
 
-#   if defined(__ARM_ARCH_7__)
+#   if (defined(__ARM_ARCH) && __ARM_ARCH >= 7) || defined(__ARM_ARCH_7__)
 #      define Q_PROCESSOR_ARM      7
 #      define Q_PROCESSOR_ARM_V7
 
-#   elif defined(__ARM_ARCH_6__)
+#   elif (defined(__ARM_ARCH) && __ARM_ARCH == 6) || defined(__ARM_ARCH_6__)
 #      define Q_PROCESSOR_ARM      6
 #      define Q_PROCESSOR_ARM_V8
 
-#   elif defined(__ARM_ARCH_5__)
+#   elif (defined(__ARM_ARCH) && __ARM_ARCH == 5) || defined(__ARM_ARCH_5__)
 #      define Q_PROCESSOR_ARM      5
 #      define Q_PROCESSOR_ARM_V5
 
